 python -m offline_doc_mcp.html_server --port 8765
 ```
 
+## What acquisition actually does (v0.1)
+
+- `project_gutenberg`: downloads the catalog CSV and writes a small metadata stub per book. It does **not** yet download book text, and `license_filter` / `mirrors` / `formats` are not applied.
+- `wikipedia_dumps` and `internet_archive_pd`: create the output folder and a README; you place dumps / `ia` downloads there yourself.
+- `process`: no-op. Only `.txt` / `.md` / `.text` files under `data/` are indexed.
+
+## Retrieval and answers
+
+`LocalIndex.search` accepts free text (it is tokenized and quoted, so punctuation and FTS operators are safe) and returns passages with `title`, `path`, `doc_id` and `chunk_index`. `Engine(archive_search=make_archive_search(index))` turns those into answers with `sources` and `evidence`. Provider answers get `truth_status` only if the provider states a valid `TRUTH_STATUS:` line; otherwise `UNKNOWN`. Provider failures set `Answer.error`.
+
+Set `OFFLINE_DOC_INDEX` to point the MCP and HTML servers at a different index file.
+
 ## Mode Isolation
 
 See `src/offline_doc_mcp/engine/modes.py` and `engine.py`.  
